{
  "_doc" : "WindowManager.windowsForBroadcast (QuipMac/Services/WindowManager.swift): which tracked windows go into a layout_update. input.windows: in tracking order, each {id, kind, enabled, onVisibleScreen}; kind is terminal (a supported terminal host), simulator (a QA-mode target) or other (any other app). input.mirrorDesktop / mirrorAllApps: the two Mac settings (both default false). input.qaPair: [idA, idB] or null. expect: the ids that are broadcast, in input order. Rules: a qaPair returns only windows whose id is in the pair; else mirrorAllApps keeps onVisibleScreen || enabled; else mirrorDesktop keeps ((terminal || simulator) && onVisibleScreen) || enabled; else enabled || (simulator && onVisibleScreen). The spec's phase-1 Windows broadcast set (enabled, plus terminals on a visible display) is the mirrorDesktop=true row without simulators. Expected values are written by the Swift test (QUIP_WRITE_VECTORS=1), never by hand.",
